 2. 🗳️ Pope makes voting history 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Photo via Getty Images Pope Leo XIV has voted in the Illinois midterm elections using a mail-in ballot, Axios' Josephine Walker reports. 

 That makes him the first sitting pope to vote in a U.S. election. ⛪️ The Holy See Press Office said in a statement that Leo "has exercised his right to vote as a United States citizen, whenever he was eligible to do so" and that "in keeping with this long-standing practice of civic participation, he has submitted his mail-in ballot in Chicago."

 The statement added that Leo believes "in the right and the duty of citizens to participate in democratic processes." 🫏🐘 Leo has voted in both Democratic and Republican primaries over the last two decades. 

